<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mysore</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Mysuru</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mysore (Mysuru) is a city in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karnataka">Karnataka</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. According to tradition it became the seat of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wadiyar-dynasty">Wodeyar dynasty</a> in 1399, and the Wodeyars rose from local chiefs under Vijayanagara to rulers of the Kingdom of Mysore. After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tipu-sultan">Tipu Sultan</a>'s fall in 1799 it was again the capital of their princely state. It is known for its palace and its Dasara festival.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mysore.jpg" alt="Mysore" width="320" height="561" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sathyaprakash01 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mysuru_Montage.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
